1
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:36,494
‎ATSUSHI MATSUYAMA - CUSTOMS OFFICER

2
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:38,747
Looks pretty rough over there…

3
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:42,292
-It's not gonna taste like my homemade.
-Passport, please. Your passport, please.

4
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:50,800
‎RAN FUKAZAWA - CHIEF HEARING OFFICER

5
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:23,041
Matsuyama, let that man through.

6
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:27,962
IMMIGRATION OFFICER (MINISTRY OF JUSTICE)
AKIHIKO SEIKE

7
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:29,506
Let him through before he suspects us.

8
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:49,109
Was it really all right to let him pass?

9
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:50,652
It's okay.

10
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,453
"That thing" has happened.

11
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,760
No more bets.

12
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:52,672
These are this week's earnings.

13
00:02:57,343 --> 00:02:58,928
Police, don't move!

14
00:02:59,012 --> 00:02:59,888
Hey!

15
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:02,891
-Hurry!
-Don't touch anything!

16
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:05,560
Don't run! Hey!

17
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:08,897
Don't move!

18
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:12,567
So this is where
the underground casino was. Okay.

19
00:03:12,650 --> 00:03:14,777
Thank you for leading us here.

20
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:22,160
So that man was the operator
of an underground casino?

21
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:24,495
And that's why he was
intentionally let through.

22
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:26,414
He spotted it in that single moment.

23
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:28,791
Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa
really is amazing.

24
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:32,128
If we had stopped him at the gate,
it probably wouldn't have led to a raid.

25
00:03:32,211 --> 00:03:34,005
Still working?

26
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:36,216
We've got one more push.

27
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,926
Four tempura soba and three duck nanban.

28
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:38,927
Okay.

29
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,970
And inari sushi as well, please.

30
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:44,349
-I'm sorry. The inari sushi is sold out.
-What…

31
00:03:44,432 --> 00:03:46,267
Look, her…

32
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:48,645
She ate all of it.

33
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:49,938
All of it?

34
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:51,814
I think she ate about ten pieces.

35
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:52,941
Coming.

36
00:03:53,691 --> 00:03:56,653
-Oh my…
-That will be 2,500 yen.

37
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:10,291
-Do you have a parking ticket?
-Yes.

38
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,671
KUUKYO

39
00:04:24,305 --> 00:04:25,390
‎KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT TERMINAL 2

40
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:33,731
Well, I'm heading off.

41
00:04:33,815 --> 00:04:36,526
Hey, are you sure I shouldn't
come with you to the airport?

42
00:04:36,609 --> 00:04:38,486
It's fine, it's fine.

43
00:04:39,529 --> 00:04:41,739
He ended up not coming home after all.

44
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:42,991
That's the same as always.

45
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:44,909
‎MAYUMI FUKAZAWA - FUKAZAWA'S WIFE

46
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:47,120
Even though his daughter is leaving
to study abroad today.

47
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:49,247
It's fine, really.

48
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:50,915
I'll tell him he should at least
see you off.

49
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:52,542
I told you, it's fine.

50
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:54,002
I'm already 17.

51
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,047
Besides, he's probably busy anyway.

52
00:04:58,131 --> 00:04:59,924
What is he, an inspection officer?

53
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:04,095
An immigration inspector. And he's
quite high up among them, you know?

54
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:09,100
Shouldn't high-up people
have more free time?

55
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:14,105
See you, Dad.

56
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:22,488
-Take care.
-Goodbye.

57
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:30,997
What? You did the raid yesterday, Iuchi?

58
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:31,956
That's right.

59
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:36,961
Man, it was a tough case.

60
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:38,963
You're straight on the promotion track.

61
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:41,007
Hey there, future Superintendent General.

62
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:43,843
Though it was thanks
to Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa.

63
00:05:43,926 --> 00:05:44,802
Actually,

64
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:49,682
one female operator from the casino
is currently on the run.

65
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:52,268
-What, she hasn't been caught yet?
-Yes.

66
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:54,228
Iuchi, you're talking too much!

67
00:05:57,148 --> 00:06:00,109
Please be very cautious
for the time being.

68
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:01,944
Understood, Superintendent General.

69
00:06:04,697 --> 00:06:07,033
Following last night's raid,
new information has come in

70
00:06:07,116 --> 00:06:08,910
from the Metropolitan Police Department.

71
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:11,037
It seems that a large shipment
of illegal drugs

72
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:14,332
worth several hundred million yen will be
brought in through this airport shortly.

73
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:18,002
-Have you identified the courier?
-Not yet.

74
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:20,963
However, there's a high probability
they hold a Japanese passport.

75
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:22,840
A Japanese national…

76
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:25,510
There might be
a major organization behind this.

77
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:27,553
If there's even
the slightest suspicious detail,

78
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:30,223
route them for inspection
regardless of nationality.

79
00:06:30,306 --> 00:06:31,140
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

80
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:34,102
We must stop those drugs coming in.

81
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:36,687
Right. We won't let even
a single gram pass.

82
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:38,648
Not even a single milligram.

83
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:39,690
-So specific.
-Okay,

84
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:10,847
-Go ahead.
-I'll check your luggage.

85
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:13,433
Go ahead.

86
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:23,443
This is quite large.

87
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:25,778
It was cheap, so I just bought it.

88
00:07:25,862 --> 00:07:27,530
It would make
a good souvenir for my niece.

89
00:07:38,916 --> 00:07:40,376
This doesn't feel like cotton.

90
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:44,547
-It's made overseas, after all.
-That's just how it's made.

91
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:48,676
I'm going to open this up.

92
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:07,862
These are cartridges
for electronic cigarettes.

93
00:08:07,945 --> 00:08:12,241
Nicotine-containing electronic cigarettes
have a set limit for personal importation.

94
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:15,620
This exceeds the regulated amount.

95
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:18,039
What, really?

96
00:08:18,122 --> 00:08:20,208
-We had no idea.
-Yes.

97
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:22,210
Do you have
an import confirmation certificate?

98
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:25,963
Forget it. We can just pay
the extra tax, right?

99
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:27,798
How much is it? How much!

100
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:30,134
I was just a bit careless!

101
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:34,305
You were careless enough to sew it in?

102
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:37,391
Next person, please.

103
00:08:37,475 --> 00:08:38,392
‎SARA NATORI - IMMIGRATION OFFICER

104
00:08:38,976 --> 00:08:39,852
Over here.

105
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:41,771
I'll take your passport.

106
00:08:48,486 --> 00:08:50,488
IMMIGRATION PASSPORT READING SYSTEM

107
00:08:52,698 --> 00:08:54,825
Please proceed.

108
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:57,245
Do you have anything to declare?

109
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:58,329
No.

110
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:02,625
Well then, welcome home.

111
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,461
Well…

112
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:11,175
That neck pillow seems quite light.

113
00:09:12,009 --> 00:09:13,469
It's made of urethane.

114
00:09:14,011 --> 00:09:15,680
May I take a look at it?

115
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:27,483
This tag says it is made of gel.

116
00:09:46,919 --> 00:09:49,505
-And this is?
-T-tea leaves!

117
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:50,673
Herbal tea, herbal tea!

118
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:53,968
No it is not. It's dried cannabis.

119
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,805
Are you serious?

120
00:09:58,472 --> 00:10:01,475
Do you normally check this carefully?

121
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:05,104
Our inspectors certainly do.

122
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:31,297
I'LL DEFINITELY BE THERE, WAIT FOR ME

123
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:35,676
You really don't have to force yourself.

124
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:39,472
-Non-stop confiscations today.
-It's a turbulent morning.

125
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:44,143
That just means Gate 24
is doing its job right.

126
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:45,561
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

127
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:47,855
What about the drugs we're looking for?

128
00:10:47,938 --> 00:10:50,191
Nothing matching that description
has been found yet.

129
00:10:50,274 --> 00:10:51,442
I see.

130
00:10:52,109 --> 00:10:53,110
Oh, that's right.

131
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:55,237
Your daughter
is leaving to study abroad today, right?

132
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,155
Yes.

133
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:58,115
Are you going to see her off?

134
00:10:58,199 --> 00:11:01,118
If I can go during my break.

135
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:02,995
You have to go.

136
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:04,997
She'll be mad at you if you don't.

137
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:08,167
Man, I hope she is just mad.

138
00:11:22,431 --> 00:11:25,059
The afternoon flights are finally done.

139
00:11:25,142 --> 00:11:27,228
Good job, everyone.

140
00:11:27,311 --> 00:11:28,771
-Shall we clean up?
-Yes.

141
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:30,314
-Yes.
-Ah, wait!

142
00:11:40,991 --> 00:11:42,201
Go ahead.

143
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:54,755
-This is our last passenger.
-Okay.

144
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:02,680
‎CHIKA KUMAGAWA - GROUND STAFF

145
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:05,015
-Allow me to assist you.
-Thank you.

146
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:09,145
Right over here, please.

147
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:17,111
-I'll take a look at your passport.
-Yes.

148
00:12:26,745 --> 00:12:28,456
Yuma Takase.

149
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:30,332
Returning from South Oserna, I see.

150
00:12:31,375 --> 00:12:32,334
Yes.

151
00:12:33,752 --> 00:12:36,881
This one says Misaki Takase.

152
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,133
My wife.

153
00:12:41,051 --> 00:12:42,219
She's here.

154
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:45,598
My condolences.

155
00:12:47,224 --> 00:12:48,309
Go ahead.

156
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:56,650
-Are those your wife's remains?
-Yes.

157
00:12:57,735 --> 00:13:02,323
During our trip, she suddenly collapsed
at the hotel, and just like that…

158
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:05,451
I see.

159
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:09,079
You can leave your luggage here.
Please proceed.

160
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:12,708
Oh…

161
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:16,629
Here…

162
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:31,435
Here, this is the death certificate

163
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:33,979
and the cremation certificate.

164
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:34,897
And this is--

165
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:37,775
-You don't need those documents here.
-Huh?

166
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:42,196
-I'm sorry.
-Are you all right?

167
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:44,073
I'll pick them up.

168
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:45,699
Ah, I'm sorry.

169
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:05,052
Ah, I'm sorry. That's mine as well.
Thank you.

170
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:22,194
Well then, may I pass through?

171
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:23,988
Of course. Right?

172
00:14:24,738 --> 00:14:26,156
Um…

173
00:14:28,325 --> 00:14:32,288
May we inspect your luggage a bit further?

174
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:34,665
-What?
-Mori?

175
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:38,085
I'm sorry. Please wait just a moment.

176
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:39,795
Mori, over here for a second.

177
00:14:42,715 --> 00:14:44,091
Natori. I'm sorry.

178
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:52,433
What do you mean, inspect the luggage?

179
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:54,059
There was something that bothered me.

180
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:58,397
Takase just lost his wife, you know?

181
00:14:58,480 --> 00:14:59,732
I understand.

182
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:02,359
However, Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa
also said

183
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:05,988
to route anyone for inspection if there's
even the slightest suspicion.

184
00:15:06,071 --> 00:15:08,449
That's true, but…

185
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:11,994
Just now, I saw inside the luggage,

186
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:14,371
and the clothes in there
were all summer clothes.

187
00:15:14,455 --> 00:15:16,665
Well, of course. It's summer right now.

188
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:19,376
South Oserna is in
the Southern Hemisphere.

189
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:21,378
It is winter there right now.

190
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:25,382
And yet, there wasn't
a single piece of winter clothing.

191
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:27,927
Yes. It is strange.

192
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:30,804
He might have disposed
of them over there, right?

193
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:32,932
-Furthermore…
-There's more?

194
00:15:33,015 --> 00:15:36,727
Takase ate a meal
at the airport before departure.

195
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:39,229
-A meal?
-How do you know that?

196
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,815
I picked up a receipt.

197
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:47,279
One cup of coffee, a large pasta,
a club sandwich, a hamburg steak,

198
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:50,658
-and cheesecake.
-No, no.

199
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:52,952
Even if you're grieving,
you still get hungry.

200
00:15:53,661 --> 00:15:58,666
Or rather, maybe he hadn't had time
to eat anything up until then.

201
00:15:58,749 --> 00:16:01,126
T-that may be so.

202
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:03,879
-However--
-It's not that I'm saying

203
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:08,258
I feel bad for Takase, so don't
inspect him, or anything like that.

204
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:09,301
It's just that

205
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:14,974
placing an additional burden on him
without clear evidence doesn't feel right.

206
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:17,977
Yes.

207
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:21,814
Well, it's true that each point
is weak on its own as evidence,

208
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:24,108
but it's also true that
strange details are adding up.

209
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:30,948
Shall we check, just to be sure?

210
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:34,785
Just to be sure.

211
00:16:40,624 --> 00:16:42,292
Excuse me.

212
00:16:47,172 --> 00:16:49,675
How much longer will this take?

213
00:16:51,093 --> 00:16:53,178
We are very sorry.

214
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:23,792
May I check that bag as well?

215
00:17:27,337 --> 00:17:28,213
Yes.

216
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:30,924
Thank you.

217
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:48,817
This medicine hasn't been declared.

218
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:53,781
I'm sorry. They're sleeping pills.

219
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:56,867
Were they prescribed by a local hospital?

220
00:17:56,950 --> 00:18:01,914
Yes. Ever since my wife passed away,
I haven't been able to sleep at all.

221
00:18:03,874 --> 00:18:06,710
Okay then, please complete
the declaration procedure later.

222
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:08,212
Yes.

223
00:18:08,295 --> 00:18:10,506
I'm truly sorry.

224
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:17,679
‎GATE 24 - SECONDARY ROOM

225
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:21,225
For now, I'm relieved that
nothing dangerous turned up.

226
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:22,351
‎Yeah.

227
00:18:22,434 --> 00:18:24,061
Are you still investigating?

228
00:18:24,144 --> 00:18:26,021
Was there anything suspicious?

229
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:29,024
No. Mori, there's no problem, right?

230
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:30,943
-No.
-Well then,

231
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:32,736
-that concludes--
-Something should be here,

232
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,863
but it is missing.

233
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:40,661
-Mori, there's no problem, right?
-No.

234
00:18:40,744 --> 00:18:43,372
-Well then, that concludes--
-Something should be here,

235
00:18:43,455 --> 00:18:45,207
-but it is missing.
-What?

236
00:18:49,503 --> 00:18:52,005
-Contact lenses?
-Yes.

237
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:54,842
They were in the deceased wife's luggage,

238
00:18:54,925 --> 00:18:58,178
but the prescription here is minus 7.00.

239
00:18:58,262 --> 00:19:00,848
Huh, that's about the same as mine.

240
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:02,724
Endo, you wear contact lenses?

241
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:05,310
Yes, if I take them out, I can't see.

242
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:07,437
That's why I always carry glasses around.

243
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:09,940
-I see.
-True, they aren't there.

244
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:14,278
Yes, there are no glasses.

245
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:18,740
If traveling, it would be natural
to bring them as a spare.

246
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:21,368
Maybe he lost them somewhere?

247
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:24,496
Besides, does him not having glasses
imply something bad?

248
00:19:25,289 --> 00:19:26,874
That, I do not know.

249
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,043
Let's just let him go already.

250
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:35,757
Takase lost his partner
and hasn't been able to sleep.

251
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:42,764
What's wrong?

252
00:19:43,348 --> 00:19:46,518
Takase was drinking coffee
before coming here.

253
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:49,354
-And it was a Robusta blend.
-Robusta?

254
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:52,566
Yes. A bean with a strong bitter taste
and high caffeine content.

255
00:19:52,649 --> 00:19:56,862
Would someone suffering from insomnia
drink such coffee right before boarding?

256
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:58,906
Yes. It is strange.

257
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:02,367
Feels like there are

258
00:20:03,118 --> 00:20:04,661
a lot of small catches, huh?

259
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:09,958
But it's not decisively suspicious, is it?

260
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:14,546
Everyone, please be careful
in dealing with the bereaved man.

261
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:17,049
It affects the credibility
of the entire gate.

262
00:20:17,132 --> 00:20:19,635
I think it's best to stop here as well.

263
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:34,524
I will guide passengers on EuroSky Airways
Flight ESA235 bound for London.

264
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:36,735
Check-in is now beginning.

265
00:20:36,818 --> 00:20:39,988
Please have your passport ready
and proceed to the check-in counter.

266
00:20:40,072 --> 00:20:41,573
TO LONDON

267
00:20:49,623 --> 00:20:52,251
-Ah, Dad!
-Here, take this.

268
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:53,794
Okay, thank you.

269
00:20:54,711 --> 00:20:56,421
Well, I'm off now.

270
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:59,591
Miss, do you know where
the check-in counter is?

271
00:21:01,009 --> 00:21:03,470
Yes, I'm fine.

272
00:21:16,566 --> 00:21:22,239
I'M GOING SOON, OKAY?

273
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:32,124
There was nothing in the luggage, right?

274
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:33,417
No.

275
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:37,379
-In that case, we should stop here--
-Well…

276
00:21:38,213 --> 00:21:42,050
There is still one place
we haven't checked.

277
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:01,361
Wait, Mori.

278
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:04,323
-You don't mean…
-There's no way we could do that.

279
00:22:04,406 --> 00:22:06,867
If we handle this wrong,
it will become a really big problem.

280
00:22:06,950 --> 00:22:08,493
We must consider his feelings.

281
00:22:09,536 --> 00:22:12,039
If it were me, I might never forgive it.

282
00:22:12,789 --> 00:22:16,543
Demanding to inspect the urn
where my wife rests…

283
00:22:20,964 --> 00:22:23,258
What do you think, Matsuyama?

284
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:24,509
Are you against it?

285
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:30,891
Actually, there's one thing bothering me.

286
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:34,936
Earlier, Takase…

287
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:43,612
It looked like he intentionally
drew our eyes to that bag.

288
00:22:44,571 --> 00:22:47,491
-Intentionally?
-I was bothered by that as well.

289
00:22:47,574 --> 00:22:50,660
Could there have been something else
he didn't want inspected?

290
00:22:50,744 --> 00:22:52,245
Meaning…

291
00:22:55,832 --> 00:22:58,835
But if we don't find anything in it…

292
00:22:59,544 --> 00:23:01,463
Takase will probably get angry at us.

293
00:23:02,089 --> 00:23:04,800
He might yell at us and hold a grudge.

294
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:07,010
Oh, no, come on…

295
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:11,681
But that's

296
00:23:12,974 --> 00:23:14,768
part of our job as well.

297
00:23:18,647 --> 00:23:19,606
Right?

298
00:23:21,441 --> 00:23:22,484
Yes.

299
00:23:23,985 --> 00:23:25,112
Hayami?

300
00:23:34,454 --> 00:23:37,582
COMING NOW, SORRY I'M LATE

301
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:47,592
She's mad, huh?

302
00:23:56,184 --> 00:23:57,185
I'm almost there.

303
00:23:57,269 --> 00:24:00,105
Ah, this is Seike.

304
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:04,985
-What's up?
-Well,

305
00:24:05,068 --> 00:24:09,614
we've decided to inspect
a passenger's urn.

306
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:16,663
Since it's a serious matter, we would
like you to be present as well.

307
00:24:19,082 --> 00:24:20,542
What is he doing?

308
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:22,627
‎…please try again later…

309
00:24:26,506 --> 00:24:27,465
Understood.

310
00:24:28,758 --> 00:24:29,885
I'll be right there.

311
00:24:42,147 --> 00:24:43,356
Let's go.

312
00:24:44,858 --> 00:24:46,276
Excuse me.

313
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:49,487
I am Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa.

314
00:24:51,281 --> 00:24:52,282
Fukazawa?

315
00:24:53,491 --> 00:24:55,202
Takase?

316
00:24:55,285 --> 00:24:58,038
-Do you know each other?
-Yes.

317
00:24:58,121 --> 00:24:59,789
We're mountain-climbing friends.

318
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:03,084
We paired up as buddies and tried
to summit together many times.

319
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:04,628
I see.

320
00:25:05,503 --> 00:25:08,673
Fukazawa helped me
on the mountains many times.

321
00:25:12,469 --> 00:25:15,764
You were reckless,
and I had to bail you out.

322
00:25:19,976 --> 00:25:21,436
I heard what happened.

323
00:25:22,896 --> 00:25:26,775
I heard about Misaki. It's unfortunate.

324
00:25:28,985 --> 00:25:29,945
Yes.

325
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:35,575
Misaki often came
to the mountaineering club as well.

326
00:25:36,284 --> 00:25:37,869
She wasn't good with the cold.

327
00:25:39,329 --> 00:25:42,207
She always said she hated snow mountains

328
00:25:42,290 --> 00:25:45,126
and would wait at the mountain lodge.

329
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:47,379
Was that so?

330
00:25:48,755 --> 00:25:50,465
You remember well.

331
00:25:52,175 --> 00:25:55,387
She was someone who valued life.

332
00:25:56,721 --> 00:25:59,224
Misaki would be pleased to hear that too.

333
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:07,357
-Hey, Takase--
-Um, please, let me go home already.

334
00:26:08,483 --> 00:26:10,527
I presented my documents and passport.

335
00:26:10,610 --> 00:26:12,529
I showed all my luggage.

336
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:14,823
What else are you doubting?

337
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:17,409
Finally,

338
00:26:19,411 --> 00:26:21,871
I would like to inspect that.

339
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:29,129
Are you serious?

340
00:26:32,716 --> 00:26:35,552
The person inside here
is Misaki, you know?

341
00:26:36,428 --> 00:26:39,389
-I am very sorry.
-Fukazawa!

342
00:26:41,474 --> 00:26:46,438
To ensure it isn't touched
more than necessary, I will be present.

343
00:27:42,994 --> 00:27:44,079
I'll open it.

344
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,555
They're quite fine.

345
00:28:02,639 --> 00:28:06,017
Depending on the country,
they crush human remains finely.

346
00:28:11,439 --> 00:28:12,732
Visually, there are no abnormalities.

347
00:28:31,251 --> 00:28:33,002
Nothing abnormal on the X-ray either.

348
00:28:58,862 --> 00:29:00,739
No drug reaction either.

349
00:29:08,371 --> 00:29:12,041
Even though it was part of my duties,
I hurt you and Misaki.

350
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:15,628
I apologize from the bottom
of my heart. I am truly sorry.

351
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:21,426
Fukazawa, please raise your head.

352
00:29:25,305 --> 00:29:28,391
Suspecting people is your job, after all.

353
00:29:29,058 --> 00:29:33,146
Nothing showed up,
so that's enough for me.

354
00:29:35,482 --> 00:29:38,985
Let me offer incense to her
next time I see you.

355
00:29:40,403 --> 00:29:43,239
Yes. Misaki will be happy too.

356
00:29:46,534 --> 00:29:47,744
Thank you for waiting.

357
00:29:49,162 --> 00:29:50,079
Thank you.

358
00:29:52,332 --> 00:29:53,249
Well then.

359
00:30:05,512 --> 00:30:06,554
Good work, everyone.

360
00:30:12,602 --> 00:30:14,145
-It's heartbreaking.
-Yes.

361
00:30:15,104 --> 00:30:17,774
Somehow, Takase not being mad at us
makes it even sadder.

362
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:08,950
I will report to the higher-ups now.

363
00:31:09,033 --> 00:31:11,202
It couldn't be helped.
It was a necessary check.

364
00:31:11,286 --> 00:31:13,454
Even so, what the higher-ups will say…

365
00:31:13,538 --> 00:31:15,331
Oh, stop complaining!

366
00:31:15,415 --> 00:31:16,875
Just brace yourselves!

367
00:31:16,958 --> 00:31:18,710
Give me a break.
I'm the one they'll scold.

368
00:31:18,793 --> 00:31:20,628
Mori? What are you doing?

369
00:31:25,008 --> 00:31:26,718
Sorry, everyone.

370
00:31:28,469 --> 00:31:32,140
Didn't think I'd run into
an acquaintance on the job.

371
00:31:32,807 --> 00:31:34,392
Um…

372
00:31:34,475 --> 00:31:35,643
What's wrong?

373
00:31:36,436 --> 00:31:39,230
I met Takase's wife…

374
00:31:42,984 --> 00:31:44,402
yesterday.

375
00:31:44,485 --> 00:31:46,613
-Huh?
-His wife?

376
00:31:46,696 --> 00:31:48,072
What do you mean?

377
00:31:48,656 --> 00:31:53,119
First, please look at this.
It was among his wife's luggage.

378
00:31:53,745 --> 00:31:57,624
This was a coaster from a casino
named "Noir" in South Oserna.

379
00:31:58,416 --> 00:32:00,001
-A casino?
-Yes.

380
00:32:00,084 --> 00:32:03,838
However, I checked, and this establishment
doesn't have an operating license.

381
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:07,634
-An underground casino?
-Most likely.

382
00:32:07,717 --> 00:32:12,013
Are you saying the Takase couple
went to that underground casino?

383
00:32:12,096 --> 00:32:14,307
It would explain why Misaki,
who is sensitive to the cold,

384
00:32:14,390 --> 00:32:18,186
went to South Oserna
without bringing winter clothes.

385
00:32:18,269 --> 00:32:20,188
She stayed in a casino the whole time.

386
00:32:20,271 --> 00:32:21,147
Yes.

387
00:32:21,898 --> 00:32:25,401
Could that be related
to Iuchi's information?

388
00:32:25,485 --> 00:32:26,653
Iuchi's?

389
00:32:26,736 --> 00:32:28,905
That a female underground
casino operator is on the run.

390
00:32:29,614 --> 00:32:32,408
-An operator?
-That, I do not know.

391
00:32:32,492 --> 00:32:35,912
However, yesterday, I saw something
at the airport's soba shop.

392
00:32:42,877 --> 00:32:45,505
A woman holding chips from this casino.

393
00:32:46,422 --> 00:32:47,674
That lady?

394
00:32:47,757 --> 00:32:49,467
How did you remember that so well?

395
00:32:49,550 --> 00:32:50,885
She ate ten pieces of inari sushi.

396
00:32:50,969 --> 00:32:53,554
-Ah, so that's why.
-A grudge over that inari sushi, huh?

397
00:32:54,138 --> 00:32:57,225
So, why do you think
that woman was Misaki?

398
00:32:57,308 --> 00:32:59,769
The casino is not the only reason.

399
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:01,813
Look at this.

400
00:33:04,190 --> 00:33:07,402
This is a towel that was
in the wife's luggage.

401
00:33:07,986 --> 00:33:11,990
That woman also had a key case
with this exact same logo.

402
00:33:14,742 --> 00:33:16,411
It is a minor heavy metal band.

403
00:33:18,413 --> 00:33:24,377
-Then the lady at the soba shop was…
-Takase's wife?

404
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:26,546
Yes. Looking at it that way,

405
00:33:26,629 --> 00:33:28,631
all the strange details connect.

406
00:33:29,298 --> 00:33:31,718
-Strange details?
-Ah.

407
00:33:31,801 --> 00:33:33,302
For example, this.

408
00:33:34,303 --> 00:33:36,556
In the wife's luggage,
there were slippers.

409
00:33:37,181 --> 00:33:39,934
However, there are no shoes
for outdoor wear.

410
00:33:40,018 --> 00:33:42,562
What was she wearing during the trip?

411
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:48,109
No shoes or glasses
in the luggage, does that mean…

412
00:33:48,192 --> 00:33:50,611
Those are things necessary for driving.

413
00:33:50,695 --> 00:33:52,488
Yes, that is correct.

414
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:55,825
Furthermore, at that time,
that woman presented a parking ticket.

415
00:33:55,908 --> 00:33:57,994
-Do you have a parking ticket?
-Yes.

416
00:33:58,077 --> 00:33:59,912
PARKING TICKET

417
00:33:59,996 --> 00:34:03,875
In other words, that woman
came to the airport by car.

418
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:07,086
Perhaps even now,

419
00:34:07,170 --> 00:34:09,088
she might be driving somewhere.

420
00:34:23,811 --> 00:34:25,563
I borrowed this from the security center.

421
00:34:25,646 --> 00:34:27,690
It's CCTV footage
from around the soba shop yesterday.

422
00:34:32,612 --> 00:34:38,326
SOBA

423
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:49,295
-That's…
-The inari sushi woman.

424
00:35:00,598 --> 00:35:02,433
-Iuchi…
-You know,

425
00:35:02,517 --> 00:35:06,020
I asked before, but could you not treat
the police like a handyman service?

426
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:08,731
Sorry, future Superintendent General.

427
00:35:09,315 --> 00:35:11,442
Well, I'll forgive you this time.

428
00:35:11,526 --> 00:35:12,860
What, you will?

429
00:35:12,944 --> 00:35:14,695
What was the result of the inquiry?

430
00:35:14,779 --> 00:35:18,074
Is this person the female casino operator
you were talking about, Iuchi?

431
00:35:18,157 --> 00:35:19,909
No, she was unrelated to that.

432
00:35:19,992 --> 00:35:22,703
However, as a result
of facial recognition matching,

433
00:35:22,787 --> 00:35:25,581
it matched the passport photo
of Misaki Takase.

434
00:35:25,665 --> 00:35:29,252
-Then…
-This woman is Misaki Takase.

435
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:35,091
-She's alive.
-Then, what was inside that urn?

436
00:35:35,174 --> 00:35:36,717
Where is Takase right now?

437
00:35:59,991 --> 00:36:01,617
-Let's go.
-Okay!

438
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:03,327
Counselor!

439
00:36:04,036 --> 00:36:07,582
Information just came in
from South Oserna Airport.

440
00:36:08,166 --> 00:36:11,586
Misaki Takase is suspected of having left
using another person's passport.

441
00:36:11,669 --> 00:36:12,753
We thought so.

442
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:15,089
Local authorities are also pursuing
her whereabouts. At this rate…

443
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:18,593
At this rate, it could become
an international incident

444
00:36:18,676 --> 00:36:21,762
because you people
didn't catch that couple.

445
00:36:22,513 --> 00:36:25,433
Why didn't you inspect them
more thoroughly?

446
00:36:25,516 --> 00:36:28,227
If we had inspected them,
you would have complained anyway.

447
00:36:28,311 --> 00:36:30,897
-Did you say something?
-No, nothing.

448
00:36:30,980 --> 00:36:32,315
Um…

449
00:36:33,441 --> 00:36:37,320
Strictly speaking, the one that overlooked
Misaki Takase's illegal entry

450
00:36:37,403 --> 00:36:40,615
was not Gate 24, but the main terminal.

451
00:36:42,158 --> 00:36:46,621
They permitted her entry without detecting
the impersonation passport.

452
00:36:47,371 --> 00:36:48,789
No, well…

453
00:36:50,499 --> 00:36:54,837
-Anyway, if this becomes any bigger--
-We know.

454
00:36:54,921 --> 00:36:57,465
-Responsibility…
-Will be taken by me.

455
00:36:58,674 --> 00:37:02,261
Anyway, right now, we stop him.

456
00:37:03,346 --> 00:37:04,347
Contact the airport police.

457
00:37:04,430 --> 00:37:06,098
-Tell them about Takase!
-Okay!

458
00:37:24,742 --> 00:37:26,202
Takase.

459
00:37:27,119 --> 00:37:28,537
-Wait!
-Spotted Takase!

460
00:37:28,621 --> 00:37:29,538
Move!

461
00:37:29,622 --> 00:37:32,375
-Move! Move!
-Takase, stop!

462
00:37:33,042 --> 00:37:34,001
Stop!

463
00:37:35,127 --> 00:37:36,337
Takase!

464
00:37:41,884 --> 00:37:45,012
Announcement for passengers
on EuroSky Airways Flight

465
00:37:45,096 --> 00:37:48,391
ESA235 bound for London.

466
00:37:48,474 --> 00:37:51,477
The security checkpoint
is currently very crowded.

467
00:37:51,560 --> 00:37:53,145
-Jeez.
-Passengers boarding this flight,

468
00:37:53,229 --> 00:37:55,606
-I'm going.
-please complete security inspection early

469
00:37:55,690 --> 00:37:57,525
-and proceed to the gate.
-Wait!

470
00:37:58,484 --> 00:38:00,695
-Takase!
-There's nowhere to run!

471
00:38:11,038 --> 00:38:12,915
Stay back. I'll really do it.

472
00:38:12,999 --> 00:38:14,667
Takase, calm down.

473
00:38:14,750 --> 00:38:15,876
Shut up! Get back!

474
00:38:19,255 --> 00:38:20,631
Tsumugi!

475
00:38:21,590 --> 00:38:22,925
Dad!

476
00:38:24,510 --> 00:38:25,428
Dad?

477
00:38:33,227 --> 00:38:34,687
Takase.

478
00:38:37,189 --> 00:38:38,733
Let her go.

479
00:38:39,900 --> 00:38:42,945
Fukazawa, please let me go.

480
00:38:43,779 --> 00:38:47,450
I needed money!
I got into heavy debt at the casino!

481
00:38:48,117 --> 00:38:50,661
Back then, you saved me, didn't you?

482
00:38:50,745 --> 00:38:52,330
On the blizzard-covered mountain,

483
00:38:52,955 --> 00:38:54,790
you didn't abandon me!

484
00:38:54,874 --> 00:38:59,253
You know the weight of a life,
so why did you mess with it?

485
00:39:06,510 --> 00:39:08,971
Don't you dare desecrate life.

486
00:39:12,683 --> 00:39:14,226
Stay back!

487
00:39:34,872 --> 00:39:36,165
Secured!

488
00:39:39,335 --> 00:39:40,669
Oh my…

489
00:39:42,588 --> 00:39:43,881
They're good.

490
00:39:50,429 --> 00:39:52,390
Are you all right, Tsumugi?

491
00:39:54,266 --> 00:39:55,309
Not at all.

492
00:39:58,562 --> 00:40:00,815
You're late, Dad.

493
00:40:33,848 --> 00:40:35,224
Welcome home.

494
00:40:35,307 --> 00:40:37,518
Hello, dear.

495
00:40:38,102 --> 00:40:41,439
You're Misaki Takase, right?
Are you here to pick up your husband?

496
00:40:50,030 --> 00:40:52,950
-I'm glad you weren't injured.
-Yes.

497
00:40:53,033 --> 00:40:55,202
Though I did stomp on the culprit's foot.

498
00:40:55,286 --> 00:40:56,370
How reliable.

499
00:40:56,996 --> 00:40:58,414
Understood, thank you.

500
00:40:59,582 --> 00:41:01,584
If you head over right now,
you'll make it in time.

501
00:41:01,667 --> 00:41:03,711
I see. Thank you.

502
00:41:05,129 --> 00:41:07,756
-Well then, I'm off.
-Yes.

503
00:41:09,008 --> 00:41:11,343
Get along with Mom, okay?

504
00:41:11,427 --> 00:41:12,887
Don't worry.

505
00:41:13,637 --> 00:41:14,555
See you.

506
00:41:18,476 --> 00:41:19,477
Go ahead.

507
00:41:38,621 --> 00:41:41,624
Looks like you really are busy.

508
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:46,378
See you, Inspector.

509
00:41:47,796 --> 00:41:50,758
-He's not an inspector, he's Chief--
-Forget it.

510
00:41:50,841 --> 00:41:51,759
See you.

511
00:41:54,303 --> 00:41:57,723
None of that stuff matters.

512
00:42:24,083 --> 00:42:27,878
The death certificate and cremation
certificate submitted by Takase

513
00:42:27,962 --> 00:42:29,838
were all forged.

514
00:42:29,922 --> 00:42:32,216
It seems the local doctor
was bribed as well.

515
00:42:33,050 --> 00:42:35,177
Going to such lengths…

516
00:42:35,261 --> 00:42:38,430
It seems the wife, Misaki, illegally
obtained another person's family register

517
00:42:38,514 --> 00:42:41,934
and returned to the country the day before
using a passport under that name.

518
00:42:42,017 --> 00:42:45,688
She intended to pretend she died
and live a new life as a different person.

519
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:49,316
Regarding that urn,

520
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:52,194
stimulant drugs were detected from inside.

521
00:42:52,278 --> 00:42:53,946
To evade inspection,

522
00:42:54,029 --> 00:42:56,448
it seems they placed human ash
at the top of the urn

523
00:42:56,532 --> 00:42:58,784
and hid the stimulant drugs underneath.

524
00:42:59,368 --> 00:43:02,913
Since what we tested was the ash
on top, no reaction came out.

525
00:43:02,997 --> 00:43:03,872
Yes.

526
00:43:03,956 --> 00:43:05,958
What was that ash, anyway?

527
00:43:06,041 --> 00:43:08,627
There is a high probability
it was animal bones.

528
00:43:09,878 --> 00:43:11,964
Really elaborate work.

529
00:43:12,965 --> 00:43:17,845
The reason we were able to figure it out
was thanks to Mori protecting the urn.

530
00:43:19,805 --> 00:43:23,475
Things are to be treated
with care, after all.

531
00:43:28,063 --> 00:43:31,900
Also, the two of them frequented
local underground casinos

532
00:43:31,984 --> 00:43:34,111
and accumulated large debts.

533
00:43:34,194 --> 00:43:38,032
It seems they were taken advantage of
and forced to work as couriers.

534
00:43:38,115 --> 00:43:41,577
The wife's death, the contents of the urn,

535
00:43:41,660 --> 00:43:44,038
it was all a lie.

536
00:43:45,122 --> 00:43:48,500
Objects do not tell lies.

537
00:43:53,422 --> 00:43:54,632
That's right.

538
00:43:55,799 --> 00:43:58,218
It's always humans who do.

539
00:44:05,976 --> 00:44:07,686
Good work, everyone.

540
00:44:07,770 --> 00:44:11,148
-It seems yesterday was quite hectic.
-This is business as usual.

541
00:44:12,399 --> 00:44:14,360
Today for sure, I'll get the inari sushi!

542
00:44:14,443 --> 00:44:16,987
I'm sorry. It's sold out today too.

543
00:44:17,071 --> 00:44:19,782
-What…
-It's remarkably popular, isn't it?

544
00:44:19,865 --> 00:44:22,076
The people over there ate all of it.

545
00:44:23,118 --> 00:44:24,244
Man…

546
00:44:28,749 --> 00:44:31,085
Ah, Mori, want some?

547
00:44:38,342 --> 00:44:39,593
Oh my…

548
00:44:44,181 --> 00:44:46,517
‎What is love?

549
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:48,769
‎What, a fake proposal?

550
00:44:48,852 --> 00:44:49,728
‎Right here?

551
00:44:49,812 --> 00:44:52,356
‎-This guy is a marriage scammer!
‎-20 million yen.

552
00:44:52,439 --> 00:44:54,775
‎I will pay for all of it.

553
00:44:54,858 --> 00:44:56,610
‎What are these two?

554
00:44:56,693 --> 00:44:58,904
‎Inspecting love?

555
00:44:58,987 --> 00:44:59,863
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
